#   - https://github.com/BlueSwordM/SVT-AV1/blob/master/Docs/Parameters.md
#   - https://colinmckellar.com/2024/01/11/video-encoder-comparison/
#   - https://salivity.github.io/ffmpeg/article/how-to-calculate-vmaf-score-using-f-fmpeg
#   - https://github.com/Netflix/vmaf/blob/master/resource/doc/ffmpeg.md
#
# Helpers:
#   AMD GPU:
#   - amdgpu_top -n 1 -J | jq (show usage of GPU :)
#   - amdgpu_top --json | jq -c -r '(.devices[] | (.Info | .DeviceName + " (" + .PCI + "): ") + ([.gpu_activity | to_entries[] | .key + ": " + (.value.value|tostring) + .value.unit] | join(", ")))'
#   - sudo amdmemtweak --current | grep -E "REF:|GPU [0-9]:" >> "${LOG}/${VIDEO_FILE_NAME}_ncnn_${NCNN_METHOD}.log" 2>&1 (memory tweaking checking - only works on older cards when BIOS is not locked)
#   - ncnn threads optimization examples:
#       - 5:45 [min] (-j 2:2,2:4)
#       - 4:03 [min] (-j 3:2,2:5)
#       - 4:07 [min] (-j 3:3,3:5)
#       - 3:09 [min] (-j 4:2,2:6)
#       - 2:01 [min] (-j 6:2,2:8, mem REF 5 & 30)
#       - 1:48 [min] (-j 8:2,2:10)
#
#   - BlueRay BDm2ts -> all streams
#       - mpls -> all details about all streams
#           mediainfo --Output=JSON 00000.mpls | jq -r '.media.track[] | select(.ID == "4769") | .Language + "," + .Format'
#
#   - Field Expected Value for HDR
#       - Transfer characteristics    PQ (SMPTE ST 2084) or HLG
#       - Bit depth   10 bits or higher
#       - Color primaries BT.2020
#           - color_space=bt2020nc
#           - color_transfer=smpte2084
#           - color_primaries=bt2020
#   - tone mapping help:
#     - bt.2390     libplacebo      ITU standard, broadcast-safe default
#     - hable       zscale tonemap  filmic curve, holds shadow + highlight detail
#     - reinhard    zscale tonemap  brighter output if hable is too dark
#     - st2094-40   libplacebo      HDR10+ with dynamic per-scene metadata
#
#   - Field Expected Value for SDR
#           - color_space=bt709
#           - color_transfer=bt709
#           - color_primaries=bt709
#
#   - tone-mapping: HDR to SDR
#       - ffmpeg -i input.mkv -vf "zscale=t=linear:npl=100,format=gbrpf32le,zscale=p=bt709,tonemap=tonemap=hable:desat=0,zscale=t=bt709:m=bt709:r=tv,format=yuv420p" -c:v libx264 -crf 20 -c:a copy output.mp4 -> encoded 1449 frames in 230.05s (6.30 fps), 153166.02 kb/s, Avg QP:4.00
#       - ffmpeg -i "peripheral_video_part_minute_045_for_test-conversion.mkv" -vf "libplacebo=tonemapping=bt.2390:colorspace=bt709:color_primaries=bt709:color_trc=bt709:format=yuv420p" -c:v libx265 -crf 0 -c:a copy "peripheral_video_part_minute_045_for_test-conversion_x265_lossless_libplacebo.mkv" -> encoded 1449 frames in 216.78s (6.68 fps), 174360.50 kb/s, Avg QP:3.30
#
#   - inverse tone-mapping: SDR to HDR
#       - ffmpeg -y -hide_banner -loglevel error -progress pipe:1 -i "${VIDEO_FILE_NAME}.mkv" -vf "zscale=primaries=bt709:transfer=linear,format=gbrpf32le,geq=r='r*2.0':g='g*2.0':b='b*2.0',zscale=primaries=bt2020:transfer=smpte2084:matrix=bt2020nc,format=yuv420p10le" -c:v libx265 -crf 0 -x265-params "hdr10=1:colorprim=bt2020:transfer=smpte2084:colormatrix=bt2020nc:master-display=G(13250,34500)B(7500,3000)R(34000,16000)WP(15635,16450)L(10000000,1):max-cll=1000,400" -pix_fmt yuv420p10le "${VIDEO_FILE_NAME}_hdr.mkv"
#       - but HOW how to get lut3d file in the first place ? ffmpeg -y -hide_banner -loglevel error -progress pipe:1 -i "${VIDEO_FILE_NAME}.mkv" -vf "lut3d=file=sdr_to_hdr_upmap.cube,zscale=primaries=bt2020:transfer=smpte2084:matrix=bt2020nc,format=yuv420p10le" -c:v libx265 -crf 0 -x265-params "hdr10=1:colorprim=bt2020:transfer=smpte2084:colormatrix=bt2020nc:master-display=G(13250,34500)B(7500,3000)R(34000,16000)WP(15635,16450)L(10000000,1):max-cll=1000,400" -pix_fmt yuv420p10le "${VIDEO_FILE_NAME}_hdr.mkv"
#
#   - VMAF score - quality of encoding:
#       - example: ffmpeg -i reference.mkv -r 20 -i encoded.mkv -lavfi "[0:v]setpts=PTS-STARTPTS[reference];[1:v]setpts=PTS-STARTPTS[distorted];[distorted][reference]libvmaf=log_fmt=json:log_path=/tmp/turniej_rumba.json:model='path=/usr/share/model/vmaf_v0.6.1.json':n_threads=24" -f null -
#       - example: ffmpeg -i encoded.mkv -i reference.mkv -lavfi libvmaf -f null - -> gives VMAF score
#   Score Range:
#       - VMAF scores range from 0 to 100, where 0 represents the lowest possible quality and 100 represents identical quality to the reference.
#       - A score of 93 to 95 is generally considered the threshold for "broadcast quality" or "visually lossless," meaning the average viewer cannot distinguish the compressed video from the source.


